            "y": 1
          },
          "id": 2,
          "options": {
            "content": "**Purpose.** Separates the two kinds of backlog after checkout. The **people backlog** is tasks waiting for warehouse staff. The **system backlog** is events waiting in the pipeline.\n\n**Use it when** orders aren't being dispatched fast enough, or the overview shows event age over 2 min.\n\n**How to read it**\n- People backlog: if dispatch stays below arrivals, the backlog grows. Oldest age and step duration show which step (pick, pack, dispatch) is the bottleneck.\n- System backlog: event age over 2 min, rising consumer lag or Debezium behind source means the pipeline is behind, not the staff.\n- DLQ publishes and stream restarts are failures, not delays. Click a series to open that service.\n\n**Background:** [Dashboard best practices](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/dashboards/build-dashboards/best-practices/) \u00b7 [Dashboards that matter](https://kindatechnical.com/microservices-architecture/building-observability-dashboards-that-matter.html) \u00b7 [Per-service dashboards (Google Cloud)](https://docs.cloud.google.com/stackdriver/docs/solutions/slo-monitoring/ui/svc-dashboard)",
            "mode": "markdown"
          },
          "repeatDirection": "h",
          "title": "",
          "transparent": false,
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "title": "About this dashboard",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
